<section class="hero paper-section">
  <div class="shell hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <span class="kicker">Hello from Tangerang <span aria-hidden="true">☺</span></span>
      <h1>I’m Jody.<br>I find the things<br><em>software tries to hide.</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">Security researcher, bug hunter, and curious builder. I use source code, LLMs, and a stubborn amount of testing to turn odd behavior into clear, reproducible proof.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="<%= base('/discoveries/') %>">See selected work <span>↘</span></a>
        <a class="text-link" href="mailto:jodyritonga@gmail.com">jodyritonga@gmail.com ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="hero-note" aria-label="A note about Jody">
      <svg class="portrait-doodle" viewBox="0 0 420 360" role="img" aria-label="Hand-drawn desk with a laptop, coffee, and curious eyes">
        <path d="M38 282c78-13 182-16 340 0M112 278l-16 54m218-54 22 54M128 144h170l-18 113H146zM174 257v22m79-22v22m-96 1h112"/>
        <path d="M162 175c16-18 35-18 50 0 16-18 35-18 50 0-14 30-35 42-50 45-17-3-37-15-50-45Z"/>
        <circle cx="195" cy="180" r="4"/><circle cx="229" cy="180" r="4"/>
        <path d="M57 218c5-18 13-27 27-27s23 9 27 27v38H57zM63 191c2-19 9-29 21-29s20 10 22 29M57 232H40m71 0h18"/>
        <path d="M321 159c24 10 37 27 40 51m-44-24c27 8 41 22 46 40" class="blue-line"/>
        <path d="M339 139l14 18-22 2" class="blue-line"/>
      </svg>
      <p class="hand-note">currently looking at<br><strong>browser + Android boundaries</strong></p>
      <span class="tape" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </aside>
  </div>
  <div class="shell quick-facts" aria-label="Quick facts">
    <span><b><%= @discoveries.length %></b> public CVEs</span>
    <span>browser · mobile · web</span>
    <span>human-led, LLM-assisted</span>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section work-section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><span class="section-number">01</span><h2>Selected work</h2></div>
      <p>A few vulnerabilities I found and disclosed responsibly. The official vendor records are linked—receipts are better than adjectives.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="work-list">
<% @discoveries.first(3).each_with_index do |discovery, index| %>
<%= discovery_row(discovery, index: index + 1) %>
<% end %>
    </div>
    <a class="button quiet" href="<%= base('/discoveries/') %>">View all public work <span>→</span></a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section about-preview">
  <div class="shell about-preview-grid">
    <div class="section-heading stacked"><div><span class="section-number">02</span><h2>What I do</h2></div></div>
    <div class="service-notes">
      <article><span class="hand-note">look closer</span><h3>Vulnerability research</h3><p>I trace attacker-controlled input across trust boundaries until the code either proves a real impact—or proves me wrong.</p></article>
      <article><span class="hand-note">make it useful</span><h3>Security tooling</h3><p>I build small, practical workflows that make source review, Android testing, and evidence collection more dependable.</p></article>
      <article><span class="hand-note">stay honest</span><h3>Responsible disclosure</h3><p>I care about exact versions, clean reproduction, guarded controls, and reports that make a fix easier to ship.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="contact-band">
  <div class="shell contact-grid">
    <div><span class="hand-note">a tiny internet door →</span><h2>Have an interesting<br>problem to pull apart?</h2></div>
    <div><p>I’m open to thoughtful security research, source review, and collaborations where proof matters.</p><a class="button primary" href="mailto:jodyritonga@gmail.com">Write me a note <span>↗</span></a></div>
  </div>
</section>
